people who've done very well, are in absolute despair about all this. There's a real sense of panic, of moral and political panic among the propertied classes because they've got their bribe offer from Mrs Thatcher, but they basically know that the Tories aren't going to get in. So the polls are definitely against the Tories? Oh, very much so. Very much so. So Labour have a lead of about 8% to 10% going into the campaign because Ted Heath is disregarded as, he's like a football manager who just can't win a game, Tom. Now, you may be wondering, what's happened to our old friends, the Liberals?

